  "sourceState": "Revision 1 preserves the pinned TypeScript reactive tier and .NET integrity tier as one deterministic module. The tiers share a 74-case corpus, closed operator catalog, canonical outcome vocabulary, injected clock, exact-decimal money behavior, and fail-closed resource limits. Native suites pass 201 TypeScript and 148 .NET cases; parsed canonical outcomes are structurally identical across tiers. The npm identity is preserved. The frozen HLF-055 target now uses the converged Harborline.Foundation.RuleEngine NuGet, assembly, and API identity. Host DI convenience and the broad Forms integration test remain outside this package; the latter is retained for the Forms gate. Revision 7 (T-1194, ADR-0153) adds some/all/none with element-local predicates and Enumerable.Any/All/!Any empty-array semantics, plus startsWith/endsWith with ordinal case-sensitive string semantics, in both tiers. The 16-file, 285-case shared corpus includes 106 independent literal cases for the new operations, nesting, invalid operands, exclusions, and budget exhaustion. Only the views-ck-14 borrower probe and its production declaration gain these operations; all other released borrower declarations remain unchanged.",
